}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":37,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The repaired network brings dev TTS from 47.9 down to **45.2 veh-h**, close to the 44.8 the network scored with every detector working. `work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are all written.\n\n**What I changed and why:**\n1. **Stand-in for the dead detector.** The network now treats both W2 inputs as `0.5·d_E2 + 0.25·(1 − phase3)`, built into its first layer by hand. E2, the east left-turn pocket, has the same demand and the same green phase as W2. The 0.5 shrinks for the weak correlation between opposite pockets. The 0.25 keeps the estimate near the pocket's average outside its own green, and is the smallest value that still makes an empty network visit phase 3.\n2. **Drain-deadlock fix.** Even with all detectors working, the trained network never serves some lone cars at the end of an episode, so they wait until the 30-minute cap. I rewired its least important first-layer unit into a \"only E/W through cars waiting, go to phase 2\" detector, with compensation so normal decisions barely change. Offline checks with synthetic states now clear all 2,940 near-empty test cases, against 797 failures for the original.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 364 of 7,428 (limit 371).\n\n**Simulator calls:** 3 of 5.\n- Call 1, stand-in only: 45.9, but 1–8 cars were left at the cap in 4 of 9 episodes.\n- Call 2, delivered weights: 45.2 (low 35.0, nominal 45.4, high 55.2), no cars left.\n- Call 3, same with a 1.0 coefficient: 45.2, a tie, so I kept 0.5.\n\n**Test predictions:** low 35.2, nominal 45.6, high 55.6.","ttft_ms":2500,"type":"result","duration_ms":1070350,"uuid":"65112483-f452-45c0-89da-9af8e8fad935","ttft_stream_ms":2304,"time_to_request_ms":55,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":9,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"i